    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d876">

                <pb facs="0830" n="740" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg740"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/921</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-05"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 5, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The French Ambassador called
                    this afternoon to say that the French Government has received information from
                    the French Consul at Helsingfors and from other sources that the Bolsheviki are
                    about to declare that they will not object to the independence of Finland. If
                    these are the facts the French believe that it would be the best policy to
                    recognize Finland instantly in order to prevent Germany from being the first of
                    the belligerent powers to recognize. France, however, inquires how this
                    Government feels.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d876-f1"/></p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W.
                        Phillips</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d876-f1" n="1" xml:id="d876-f1-content">
                <p>Note in the margin of MS.: “Consulted Sec’y and advised Ambassador that U. S. had
                    no plans for immediate recognition Finland and no information as to attitude of
                    Bolsheviki <hi rendition="#italic">re</hi> Finland.—W[illiam]
                        P[hillips].”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
